WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.393
- A lot of people watching
right now are like,

00:00:01.393 --> 00:00:03.430
"But social's not working for me."

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.135
And I'm like, "The
creative is the variable."

00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:07.450
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.893
You got your perspective.

00:00:12.014 --> 00:00:14.614
I just want to be happy,
don't you want to be happy?

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.760
- All right, first up,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.780
we're kicking off the show
with Shark, Barbara Corcoran.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.580
Her credits include straight
Ds in high school and college.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.090
She had 20 jobs by the time she turned 23.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.810
And then she borrowed $1,000,
quit her job as a waitress,

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.400
and started a tiny real estate
company in New York City

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.560
that is now a $5,000,000,000
real estate business.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.780
Welcome Barbara!

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:42.880
- Hey, my pleasure to be here.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.460
I love Gary, I'll do anything for him.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.530
- Barbara, it's great to see you.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.570
It's always great to see you.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.850
Happy holidays and pending new year.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.760
We don't have a lot of time,
so I'm gonna get right into it

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.650
cause I know a lot of people were excited

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.483
that you were gonna be on the show,

00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:57.370
so thanks for kicking us off.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.153
In your opinion, which
consumer behavior shift

00:01:00.153 --> 00:01:04.670
will be key to driving growth in 2021?

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.240
- Am I allowed to pick more than one?

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.073
- Yes.
- Cause I think there's

00:01:07.073 --> 00:01:08.420
probably four or five out there, okay.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.253
- Yes you are.

00:01:09.253 --> 00:01:10.590
- Number one, the customer's in charge.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.620
I think if we didn't
understand that before,

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.184
we certainly understand it now.

00:01:14.184 --> 00:01:17.580
The behavior that we
collaborate with the customer

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.220
is over with, they're
in charge, end of story.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.230
So I think the key here as an entrepreneur

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.400
is you have to stay very
close to your customer.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.120
Listen hard and see what they need.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.690
And I think the first thing
they need is they want safety.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.400
And that ain't gonna go away either.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.510
And when I say safety, I think
you have to put safety first.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.990
Customers demand it,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.650
and you don't have to worry
about how to pay for it.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.390
Because you can't afford to
worry about how to pay for it,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.160
you just have to do it.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.300
I think social media is the
fastest and cheapest way

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.971
to communicate what the safety measures

00:01:49.971 --> 00:01:52.170
your particular business has done.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.500
And I think the social
distancing protocols

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.100
that we've all recently encountered

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.830
are here to stay as well.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.360
Things like the dots on the floor,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.108
I don't expect them to go
away next year at this time.

00:02:03.108 --> 00:02:06.290
Mounted thermometers at restaurant doors.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.330
Discretionary masks for travel.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.700
I think it's all, we're gonna
just see a softer version

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.270
of the same old and it
ain't gonna go away.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.050
But safety is what people care about now

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.010
and they will continue-
- How, how,

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.927
how long do you, let
me jump in on that one.

00:02:18.927 --> 00:02:19.790
- Yeah.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.700
- You know, okay, so we see a softening,

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.950
let's say a year from today.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.501
Do you think, do you see a time

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.950
where we go back to 2019 levels?

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.340
Or do you think this is
now stuck in our culture

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.820
for quite a long time?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.100
- It's part of our culture,
it's not gonna go away.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.820
Would you travel in an airplane,

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.890
whether your traveling
business class or coach,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:41.730
and not wear a mask?

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.420
I wouldn't, never again.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.190
I mean, I kind of wanted to do that

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.500
when people were coughing next to me

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.778
but I thought it was socially rude.

00:02:47.778 --> 00:02:50.350
Nope, I'm going on the airplane
with a mask forevermore.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.780
I don't want to catch what's going around.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.570
You know, nothing's gonna go away totally.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.160
We'll have a residual that will become

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.540
part of our culture, definitely.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.930
- Understood, keep going.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.880
- Okay, online shopping is king.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.450
I mean, I almost feel
embarrassed to say that.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.110
Everybody knows that, okay.
- Yeah.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.340
- But I think part and parcel of that

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.760
is you need to go to
where the customer is.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.940
I have one business named
Cousins Maine Lobster,

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.287
a large franchise of lobster trucks.

00:03:12.287 --> 00:03:13.600
- Yes, I like those guys.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.138
- Yeah, those guys, I think
you interviewed Sabin-

00:03:15.138 --> 00:03:15.971
- Yeah.

00:03:15.971 --> 00:03:17.727
- Yeah, a smart entrepreneur.
- Smart.

00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:21.810
- But the moment Covid
hit, that guy had pivot,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.650
I hate the word pivot
but I'll have to use it

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.860
because I don't know what to substitute.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.000
Oh, he turned his business around,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.530
there's a new substitute I can use.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.720
With contactless pickup,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.384
communicating where his
trucks are gonna be,

00:03:32.384 --> 00:03:35.080
and he moved his trucks
out of the normal places

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.726
that were crowded and he utilized

00:03:36.726 --> 00:03:40.010
every single large
shopping mall parking lot.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.880
Gave people numbers, they waited in line,

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.630
picked up, they went home
with their dinner out,

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:47.100
and his increase in sales
went through the roof

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.093
within a month and a half.

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:50.690
Pretty sharp, but he
understood that he needed to go

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.951
to where the customer
was comfortable being.

00:03:52.951 --> 00:03:56.310
I also have a business that's
my most successful business

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.680
named Comfy, and what it
is is a wearable sweatshirt

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.638
and what they did is they
had $150,000,000 in sales

00:04:02.638 --> 00:04:05.790
in big box stores that
were sent back to them

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.180
when Covid hit because the big box stores

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.780
they were merchandising to had closed.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.000
What were they gonna do?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.174
They increased their sales
online, turned up a website

00:04:15.174 --> 00:04:18.300
that they hadn't taken
seriously as before,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.727
and they turned a $150,000,000 in sales

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:23.350
into $250,000,000 in sales.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.330
They went to where the
customer wanted to be,

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.770
that's exactly what they did.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.720
And then also, again obvious
so I hesitate to say it,

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.161
social media is the name of the game.

00:04:32.161 --> 00:04:34.890
I mean, I don't invest in a
single business this season

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.553
on Shark Tank unless I
felt that the entrepreneur

00:04:37.553 --> 00:04:40.850
was almost a borderline
genius on social media

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.044
because I know were gonna have to rely

00:04:42.044 --> 00:04:44.960
on the social media platforms forevermore

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.280
because we have spoiled
our customers with this

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.540
and they want it.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:52.500
In social media, I think key
traits or key entrepreneurs,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.140
or pardon me, key employees
that all of us need

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.410
as entrepreneurs are now the producers,

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:00.280
the storytellers, the videographers,

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.900
it's really become the new norm.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.610
They used to be extra people.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.460
It was nice, a luxury feature if you want.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.357
But with social media
being the name of the game

00:05:07.357 --> 00:05:09.720
it's not the case anymore.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:10.700
- Barbra, real quick on that.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.173
I'm sorry to interrupt.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.820
When you were building
your real estate empire,

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:18.032
so much of it to do with branding,

00:05:18.032 --> 00:05:21.797
was direct mail a very
strong pillar for you

00:05:21.797 --> 00:05:24.290
in the prime of your growth?

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.210
- Yes it was but,
everyone used direct mail,

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.590
but the way I was able to become

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:31.570
extremely successful with it

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.540
is that I used postcards

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.450
because I watched people
at home, including myself,

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.430
and I didn't open junk mail.
- Right.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.120
- But a postcard I was forced to read.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.670
That's what we used, yes.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:44.330
- So you paid, you paid higher

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:46.040
to be your individual postcard

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.850
versus maybe in a value
pack and you feel like

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.060
even though you were paying more

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.710
to get into a mailbox, you
were getting seen more often

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.233
and that gave you a leg up?

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.782
- It gave me a leg up but honestly

00:05:58.782 --> 00:06:00.920
I never considered value packs

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.880
cause I'm too selfish, I want
my own stage wherever I am

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.520
and I got in on a postcard.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.630
What was more effective
than the postcard campaigns

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.250
I constantly ran, was buying billboards

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.584
10 cents on the dollar.

00:06:13.584 --> 00:06:17.130
- Remnant inventory, right?
- Remnant inventory.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.990
- I did the same thing
for one of my brands.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.100
- In New York and that put my
brand frontline and center,

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.370
billboards were the king.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.530
And then also what a lot
of people didn't know then

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.010
that I took full advantage of,

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.907
was I bought remnant space
in the New York Times

00:06:28.907 --> 00:06:33.870
and the Wall Street Journal
previously saved for retailers.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.269
But when I checked into their rules,

00:06:35.269 --> 00:06:37.953
retail was not the rule,
it was just ShopRite

00:06:37.953 --> 00:06:39.427
and everybody was using them,

00:06:39.427 --> 00:06:41.760
and I started putting
full page advertisements

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.940
for all my properties
that looked at a billion

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.410
when I really had 10 cents on
the dollar on that as well.

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:50.760
- It's funny, I really think
your career and knowing it,

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.620
being an east coast guy, you know,

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:55.240
a lot of people think
about me with social media

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.330
but I got my chops in direct mail,

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.971
print, outdoor, radio-
- Wow.

00:06:58.971 --> 00:07:02.650
- Cause I was advertising as
like a kid for my dad's store.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:06.190
And I think the reason
social was so natural to me

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.430
was all the things I learned
between distribution,

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:10.390
under-priced, you just
basically talked about

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.980
under-priced attention.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:14.348
You would buy more strategically

00:07:14.348 --> 00:07:16.420
around places that people would look.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.331
You took advantage of the remnant cost.

00:07:18.331 --> 00:07:21.860
I did the same exact
stuff on print and outdoor

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.510
and direct, you couldn't really do it

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:24.366
the same way on direct mail,

00:07:24.366 --> 00:07:26.360
but the other thing I
learned during that year

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.930
cause I was doing so much of it,

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:30.010
was the creative was the variable.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.050
Even though I was buying the
full page New York Times ad

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.860
in the dining section
at a really good price

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.170
cause I knew when to buy it and how,

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.905
my ad mattered to how
many people I would get

00:07:39.905 --> 00:07:42.780
and I think that that is a big...

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.797
A lot of people watching
right now are like,

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.170
"But social's not working for me."

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.590
And I'm like, "The
creative is the variable."

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:52.160
- And the creative also must
have the key ingredient,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.780
and I'm sure you'd agree with me.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.210
It has to be authentic.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.272
People see through the bullshit now,

00:07:57.272 --> 00:07:59.450
you know, if your story's not authentic,

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.350
if you don't connect
with them on some basis.

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:04.510
I've even gotten rid of
makeup in most of my postings

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:05.900
cause I find that people respond better

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.399
to me looking ugly than
to me all dolled up.

00:08:07.399 --> 00:08:08.460
(Gary chuckles)
(hands clap)

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.760
Authentic is key

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.920
and I don't think that's gonna
change either, of course.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:13.753
- I agree with you.

00:08:13.753 --> 00:08:14.620
You got one parting shot?

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:16.400
We got a minute, I know
these are going quick.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.630
- Okay, so one more thing?
- Please.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.230
- You need to be an entrepreneur
that thrives on change.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.810
I mean, if you don't welcome
change and look for it,

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.337
seek it out like a missile like,

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:26.530
"What's next? What's next?"

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:28.594
Like a kid with a curiosity box, right?

00:08:28.594 --> 00:08:30.767
You're not gonna be ready
for the changes out there.

00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:33.240
I mean, change for me, and I don't think

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.280
I'm imagining this happening
probably twice the rate

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.900
it would four years ago,
and if your not aware

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:40.130
that today is the single best opportunity

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.556
you're ever gonna see
again for the next 10 years

00:08:42.556 --> 00:08:45.154
of taking over your
competitors market place.

00:08:45.154 --> 00:08:47.639
His beat, cause you can outperform him,

00:08:47.639 --> 00:08:50.110
out-create him, outdo
whatever you have to do

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:51.480
to get rid of that guy.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.740
This is the time to do it.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:55.140
The best time to move ahead
is always in the worst times.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:56.650
Any smart entrepreneur will tell you

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:58.380
they moved ahead in the worst times

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.193
because the big guys
are asleep at the wheel-

00:09:00.193 --> 00:09:01.736
- They get tight, they get tight.

00:09:01.736 --> 00:09:03.389
- You got it.
- Most people go on defense.

00:09:03.389 --> 00:09:05.793
- It's the time to wake up.

00:09:05.793 --> 00:09:08.070
- Barbara, it's great to see you.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:08.960
- Okay, my pleasure.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.410
- Thank you so much for
this 10 minutes, really.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.800
- Thank you very much.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.148
- YouTube watcher, what's up, it's Gary V.

00:09:14.148 --> 00:09:15.700
First of all, thank you so much.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.530
I hope you're doing super
well during these times.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.330
I also want to ask you, please subscribe

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.471
because my commitment and
exploration of YouTube

00:09:24.471 --> 00:09:25.730
is about to explode.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.380
Stories, polls, more
content, more engagement,

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.565
more surprise and delight.

00:09:29.565 --> 00:09:32.300
This is the time to subscribe.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.750
I hope you consider it
and I hope I see you soon.

